  "findings": [
    "The deterministic 2000 policy reaches the four command bounds by 9.1 s and keeps requesting outward motion; applied increments are zero. No object contact occurs during this replay.",
    "All four saved evaluation trajectories keep q4 positive, while the target is q4=-162.5 total degrees. They never enter the task C-shape condition.",
    "All 2000 printed training entries have zero grasp/lift/hold reward; these are rounded batch summaries, not raw episode event counters.",
    "With terminal potential zero, discounted q shaping telescopes to -Phi(initial). All four actual evaluations confirm -0.3280404, despite different q errors.",
    "The action penalty uses actual increments after joint-bound clipping, so persistent outward requests at the bounds cost zero in that term.",
    "Reported learned action std drops from .5 to .08. The 2000 actor mean at the final frame is [-.871,1.030,-.766,.702], consistently toward the bounds."
  ],
  "causal_interpretation": "Sparse positive grasp experience, policy-invariant q shaping without imitation, and cheap bound-saturated actions are consistent with a safe-failure local policy. This explains the observed stall, but does not prove a unique causal contribution of each design choice.",
